WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.890
After 10 years, Apple has finally updated
the design of their MacBook Air with the brand

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:08.980
new 2018 model, and from the looks of it,
it’s the best choice if you’re trying

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:11.490
to buy an entry-level MacBook, right?

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:12.490
Well not exactly.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:16.880
The new MacBook Air has some pretty serious
shortcomings compared to last years’ 13”

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:22.680
MacBook Pro, which is now on sale for $100
off for a limited time on B&amp;H, so it’s exactly

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.210
the same price as the new MacBook Air.

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:30.250
We think the 2017 MacBook Pro is the better
choice, but of course, both laptops have their

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:33.690
strengths, so let’s take a look at what
the Pro does better first.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:37.590
Even though the new MacBook Air finally has
a retina display with the same resolution

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:39.870
that the Pro has, it’s actually much worse.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:45.589
The new Air is rated at 300 nits of brightness
but LaptopMag measured only 234.

00:00:45.589 --> 00:00:53.410
In comparison, the 2017 MacBook Pro is rated
at 500 nits and it measured in at 458 nits,

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:55.500
that’s almost twice as bright!

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:59.730
You can see both laptops at maximum brightness,
and the difference is perfectly clear.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:04.170
Not only that, but the MacBook Pro supports
P3 wide-color gamut, so it’s much more color

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.700
accurate than the new Air.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:08.940
Another drawback to the new Air is the lack
of performance.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:13.409
The Pro scored quite a bit better in Geekbench
4’s CPU test, and we saw the same thing

00:01:13.409 --> 00:01:16.140
in Cinebench R15’s CPU test.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:21.899
For graphics, the Pro was 50% faster in Geekbench
4 and ____ faster in Cinebench’s graphics

00:01:21.899 --> 00:01:22.899
test.

00:01:22.899 --> 00:01:25.840
Now I know, that’s why it’s called the
Pro, but you can buy the Pro for literally

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:27.850
the same exact price as the Air.

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:32.689
Also, the new MacBook Air only comes with
a 30W power adapter, while the Pro comes with

00:01:32.689 --> 00:01:37.729
a 61W power adapter, so the battery on the
Pro should charge almost twice as fast.

00:01:37.729 --> 00:01:42.680
The trackpad on the MacBook Pro is also significantly
larger even though the keyboards are practically

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:45.729
the same size, so you’ve got more room to
navigate.

00:01:45.729 --> 00:01:49.820
One thing we noticed is that the speakers
on the 2017 Pro are actually better than the

00:01:49.820 --> 00:02:11.190
ones on the new Air, just listen for yourself.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:15.360
Based on everything we’ve compared so far,
the MacBook Pro looks like the obvious choice,

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.080
but now let’s talk about some of the ways
the MacBook Air is better.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:22.130
The Air is rated at 12 hours of battery life
while the Pro only gets 10.

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:27.220
It’s also more portable, weighing in at
2.75 pounds, a quarter of a pound less than

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:28.220
the Pro.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:32.170
Even though they’re basically the same size
if you look at them from above, the Air definitely

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:34.860
looks thinner from the side thanks to the
wedge shape.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:38.980
Interestingly, the Air is slightly thicker
at the wide end, but much thinner near the

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:39.980
front.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:44.190
The MacBook Pro’s front edge tends to dig
into your wrist after long typing sessions,

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:48.350
but the Air actually slopes downward so it’s
much more comfortable to type on.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:53.140
Not only that, but the Air has updated third-generation
butterfly keys that include a silicon barrier

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:57.830
to protect the key switches debris, which
caused issues with a rare number of older-gen

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:00.710
keyboards like on the 2017 MacBook Pro.

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:04.660
The Air also gets Touch ID, which is really
nice for logging into your account and buying

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:05.960
things with Apple Pay.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:07.450
The Pro doesn’t get that.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:11.700
The Air also comes with Apple’s new T2 Chip,
which enables Hey Siri support and takes care

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:15.960
of a lot of tasks like automatic file encryption,
which will help it stay future-proof for years

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:16.960
to come.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:20.210
However, there’s been a lot of backlash
over it, with many people complaining that

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:24.500
the T2 chip blocks third-party shops from
doing repairs on it, but to me, it’s not

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:25.540
a big deal at all.

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:26.780
So which one should you buy?

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:30.950
Well, if you care about performance, especially
graphics performance, then definitely buy

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:31.950
the Pro.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:35.652
If you use MacBook outside or constantly set
your brightness to max, then definitely buy

00:03:35.652 --> 00:03:36.652
the Pro.

00:03:36.652 --> 00:03:39.520
If you’re big on portability, honestly,
there’s not much a difference.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:43.230
They’ll both still fit in the same carrying
case and you won’t really notice the difference

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:44.230
in weight.

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:47.400
If you absolutely must get the best battery
life, then the Air is the obvious choice,

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.590
and if you do tons of typing every day, then
the Air will be more comfortable, but I own

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:55.640
a MacBook Pro and the edge doesn’t really
bother me, and I do love the larger trackpad

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:56.800
on the Pro as well.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:00.440
Another plus for the Air is that the keyboard
will be more reliable thanks to the silicon

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:04.510
barrier, and if you love having loud and clear
speakers, the Pro wins there.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:08.630
Touch ID is nice, but I honestly don’t think
it’s a big enough deal to affect someone’s

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:09.630
decision.

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:13.240
The T2 chip is nice, but I don’t think it’s
a big deal either, and I basically never use

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:16.100
the Hey Siri function on my new 2018 MacBook
Pro.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:19.930
So if you’re still having a hard time deciding
which model to buy, tally up all of the things

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:23.400
I mentioned and whether they’re important
to you or not, and then just buy the one that

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.400
gets the most points.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:28.120
We’ve got links to both in the video description,
including the link to the hundred dollars

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:32.600
off MacBook Pro sale, but it’s only for
a limited time, so make your decision quick!

